WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.120
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.390 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.360 --> 01:37.509
[Episode 56]

4
01:38.490 --> 01:41.289
[Magu Mountain Area, Bijie, Guizhou]

5
01:38.680 --> 01:41.590
How many poor people are there in the world?

6
01:42.000 --> 01:43.330
Out of every ten people,

7
01:43.500 --> 01:45.300
at least nine are poor.

8
01:43.970 --> 01:45.240
[Zhou Suyuan, Commander of the Guizhou Anti-Japanese National Salvation Army]

9
01:45.320 --> 01:46.710
[Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt, British Missionary]

10
01:45.640 --> 01:47.120
Even I, a former KMT lieutenant general who was captured,

11
01:46.820 --> 01:49.650
[Zhang Zhenhan, Former Lieutenant General and Commander of the KMT's 42nd Division]

12
01:47.120 --> 01:47.780
left my post

13
01:48.120 --> 01:50.120
and came the Red Army to save myself.

14
01:50.789 --> 01:51.870
Mr. Zhou,

15
01:52.310 --> 01:54.640
you formed three detachments

16
01:54.789 --> 01:57.789
in just over 10 days as commander of the Anti-Japanese National Salvation Army.

17
01:57.789 --> 02:00.710
You brought more than 5,000 men into the Red Army,

18
02:00.710 --> 02:03.310
and established more than 30 peasant associations.

19
02:03.310 --> 02:06.310
Your efforts caused quite a stir throughout Guizhou.

20
02:07.230 --> 02:09.910
So you believe He Long's army

21
02:10.190 --> 02:11.650
will win the future world?

22
02:11.950 --> 02:13.210
He Long is a Communist.

23
02:13.390 --> 02:14.720
He believes in Marxism.

24
02:15.000 --> 02:16.530
There are many other groups

25
02:16.590 --> 02:18.920
around the world that believe in Marxism.

26
02:19.079 --> 02:20.240
Let's put it this way.

27
02:20.240 --> 02:22.960
If the poor want to change their fate,

28
02:23.360 --> 02:26.360
ultimately, they'll have to follow the Communist Party.

29
02:26.360 --> 02:28.079
That's why Marx said,

30
02:28.470 --> 02:31.240
"The proletarians have a world to win."

31
02:31.480 --> 02:33.520
I don't know whether Marx was right.

32
02:33.960 --> 02:35.360
As missionaries,

33
02:35.390 --> 02:36.870
we put our faith in God.

34
02:36.950 --> 02:39.160
But I believe God would approve

35
02:39.180 --> 02:41.300
of what the Red Army is doing.

36
02:41.470 --> 02:44.750
Then what's your understanding of Marxism?

37
02:47.400 --> 02:48.350
Mr. Zhou,

38
02:49.400 --> 02:50.630
that's something I'll need to

39
02:50.630 --> 02:52.560
think carefully about before I can answer.

40
02:52.560 --> 02:54.840
I've actually been thinking about it for a long time.

41
02:54.840 --> 02:56.030
When I have the answer,

42
02:56.030 --> 02:57.540
I'll share it with you.

43
02:58.750 --> 03:00.350
I'm looking forward to that.

44
03:00.380 --> 03:01.570
Some of us

45
03:01.870 --> 03:03.130
believe in Communism,

46
03:03.460 --> 03:05.310
some in the Three Principles of the People,

47
03:05.310 --> 03:06.430
and others in God.

48
03:06.750 --> 03:08.630
We came from different backgrounds

49
03:08.630 --> 03:09.960
and used to argue whenever we met.

50
03:09.960 --> 03:11.750
Yet here we are, sitting together,

51
03:11.750 --> 03:13.150
having a heartfelt talk.

52
03:13.800 --> 03:15.140
It feels like a dream.

53
03:15.470 --> 03:16.470
General Yansheng (Zhang Zhenhan).

54
03:15.900 --> 03:17.940
[He Long, Corps Commander of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

55
03:16.810 --> 03:19.190
You believe in the Three Principles of the People.

56
03:19.190 --> 03:21.560
I took part in the 1911 Revolution when I was still young.

57
03:21.560 --> 03:22.600
I even served as

58
03:22.630 --> 03:25.030
the Chief Executive of the Guizhou Military Government.

59
03:25.030 --> 03:25.960
I later served as

60
03:26.030 --> 03:28.220
the Secretary-General of the Guizhou Provincial Government.

61
03:28.220 --> 03:30.360
I also believe in the Three Principles of the People.

62
03:30.360 --> 03:31.630
In 1924,

63
03:32.040 --> 03:35.040
Mr. Sun Yat-sen proposed the Three Great Policies: alliance with the Soviet Union,

64
03:35.040 --> 03:37.360
cooperation with the Communist Party, and assistance to the peasants and workers.

65
03:37.360 --> 03:38.290
But look at those

66
03:38.400 --> 03:41.000
in power today— the ruling class Marx spoke of.

67
03:41.030 --> 03:44.190
Which one of them is actually upholding the Three Principles of the People,

68
03:44.190 --> 03:46.190
let alone the Three Great Policies?

69
03:46.630 --> 03:47.710
General Yansheng,

70
03:48.329 --> 03:50.680
ironically, some of the fiercest opponents of the Red Army

71
03:50.680 --> 03:52.680
are your former classmates from the Baoding Military Academy,

72
03:52.680 --> 03:54.590
men like Bai Chongxi and He Jian.

73
03:55.280 --> 03:57.400
It's really heartbreaking.

74
03:59.470 --> 04:00.190
General He.

75
04:00.240 --> 04:01.500
I happened to overhear

76
04:01.710 --> 04:03.120
your conversation just now.

77
04:03.120 --> 04:04.520
Come on, have a seat.

78
04:05.790 --> 04:07.080
Today, our conversation around camp

79
04:07.080 --> 04:08.960
has turned into a discussion about God, Marx,

80
04:08.960 --> 04:10.800
and Mr. Sun Yat-sen.

81
04:10.840 --> 04:12.770
What an extraordinary gathering!

82
04:14.750 --> 04:15.630
I think

83
04:15.630 --> 04:18.240
people and things in this world

84
04:18.570 --> 04:20.010
are vastly different.

85
04:20.680 --> 04:23.270
But to be a true hero, a person of integrity,

86
04:23.510 --> 04:26.720
you must first be kind,

87
04:27.000 --> 04:27.800
do good deeds,

88
04:28.070 --> 04:29.330
and help those in need.

89
04:29.430 --> 04:31.510
What does it mean to be kind and do good deeds?

90
04:31.510 --> 04:33.510
Let's start with the little things:

91
04:33.790 --> 04:36.840
give a hungry person something to eat.

92
04:37.240 --> 04:38.720
When someone needs help,

93
04:38.720 --> 04:39.800
give them a hand.

94
04:40.240 --> 04:42.720
These are simple acts of kindness,

95
04:42.840 --> 04:44.070
small ways to help those in need.

96
04:44.070 --> 04:45.230
To take it a step further,

97
04:45.230 --> 04:46.390
saving someone's life

98
04:46.390 --> 04:48.630
is a greater act of helping those in need

99
04:48.740 --> 04:50.270
and a greater act of kindness.

100
04:50.270 --> 04:51.870
And on an even greater scale,

101
04:52.690 --> 04:54.550
saving our country and our people

102
04:55.200 --> 04:57.310
is the greatest act of helping those in need

103
04:57.310 --> 04:59.120
and the greatest act of kindness.

104
04:59.120 --> 05:01.360
So whether you're a missionary,

105
05:01.680 --> 05:03.070
a follower of the Three Principles of the People,

106
05:03.070 --> 05:04.190
or a Communist.

107
05:04.480 --> 05:07.000
As long as you have a kind heart, do good,

108
05:07.390 --> 05:10.210
and stand for the salvation of our country and people,

109
05:10.210 --> 05:12.260
then we're all friends.

110
05:12.680 --> 05:13.190
Right?

111
05:13.190 --> 05:14.270
Exactly.

112
05:14.630 --> 05:16.480
General He, listening to you today

113
05:16.480 --> 05:17.920
has been truly enlightening.

114
05:17.920 --> 05:18.920
I, Zhang Zhenhan,

115
05:19.040 --> 05:21.070
wouldn't presume to claim that I can save our country and people,

116
05:21.070 --> 05:23.310
but I am willing to stand with you all,

117
05:23.920 --> 05:24.950
be kind,

118
05:25.360 --> 05:26.560
do good, and work together

119
05:26.560 --> 05:28.360
toward a world of great harmony.

120
05:29.360 --> 05:30.310
Uncle!

121
05:30.530 --> 05:31.290
Xiang Xuan.

122
05:32.040 --> 05:32.440
Here.

123
05:32.470 --> 05:33.590
You guys carry on.

124
05:34.080 --> 05:34.720
Let's go.

125
05:39.870 --> 05:40.720
I, He Long,

126
05:40.870 --> 05:42.310
started my revolution with two kitchen knives

127
05:42.310 --> 05:44.360
because I couldn't bear to see the poor suffer.

128
05:44.360 --> 05:45.870
Anyone who cares about the poor

129
05:45.870 --> 05:47.159
and keeps them close to their heart

130
05:47.159 --> 05:48.040
is someone

131
05:48.480 --> 05:49.710
I'd gladly become friends with.

132
05:49.710 --> 05:53.770
I'm willing to make friends with anyone like this from all over the world.

133
05:57.680 --> 05:58.610
Let's go.

134
05:59.870 --> 06:02.090
The two kitchen knives he mentioned...

135
06:02.120 --> 06:03.450
what was that all about?

136
06:03.480 --> 06:05.080
Those who work for the people

137
06:06.000 --> 06:07.800
will always have their support.

138
06:17.040 --> 06:17.870
Xiang Xuan,

139
06:18.070 --> 06:18.930
remember this.

140
06:19.150 --> 06:20.830
From now on, don't call me Uncle

141
06:20.830 --> 06:22.430
when we're with the troops.

142
06:23.160 --> 06:24.690
Then what should I call you?

143
06:24.800 --> 06:25.680
You

144
06:26.070 --> 06:27.800
should call me Comrade He Long.

145
06:28.890 --> 06:30.350
Yes, Comrade He Long!

146
06:31.430 --> 06:32.240
All right.

147
06:32.690 --> 06:34.800
That's more like it, Comrade Xiang Xuan.

148
06:34.800 --> 06:36.800
But since no one's around,

149
06:37.150 --> 06:38.430
you can call me Uncle.

150
06:38.830 --> 06:40.240
Yes, Comrade Uncle!

151
06:41.720 --> 06:42.450
Kiddo.

152
06:43.080 --> 06:45.350
Uncle, what are we doing here?

153
06:47.830 --> 06:49.950
I need you to help me with something.

154
06:50.800 --> 06:52.690
Come on. Help me cauterize this wound.

155
06:52.690 --> 06:54.630
Uncle, are you trying to warm yourself by the fire?

156
06:54.630 --> 06:56.360
Then I'll go find some dry wood.

157
06:57.159 --> 06:58.070
Don't go.

158
06:58.270 --> 07:00.630
I need you to burn my wound.

159
07:00.830 --> 07:01.560
Here.

160
07:02.430 --> 07:03.360
Take this.

161
07:03.560 --> 07:04.800
I'm scared.

162
07:05.510 --> 07:06.840
You're scared already?

163
07:06.870 --> 07:07.830
Then how are you going to

164
07:07.830 --> 07:09.960
fight alongside me on the battlefied?

165
07:10.190 --> 07:11.120
How are you going to

166
07:11.120 --> 07:12.360
avenge your mother and your aunt?

167
07:12.360 --> 07:13.360
I just called you Comrade,

168
07:13.360 --> 07:15.090
and now you're not one anymore?

169
07:15.870 --> 07:16.950
If you don't dare, forget it.

170
07:16.950 --> 07:18.240
Go get Uncle Li for me.

171
07:19.600 --> 07:20.160
Go on.

172
07:20.290 --> 07:21.120
I can do it!

173
07:29.310 --> 07:30.150
Hold on.

174
07:36.100 --> 07:36.659
Do it.

175
07:36.690 --> 07:37.570
Are you sure?

176
07:37.870 --> 07:38.500
Go ahead.

177
07:52.820 --> 07:54.020
Light another match.

178
08:31.040 --> 08:32.000
Uncle.

179
08:32.870 --> 08:33.720
It's done.

180
08:37.780 --> 08:38.460
Good!

181
08:39.640 --> 08:42.159
Uncle, doesn't that hurt?

182
08:43.400 --> 08:45.560
Good boy. Why are you crying?

183
08:45.970 --> 08:47.920
You know, I'm not

184
08:48.420 --> 08:49.610
made of steel.

185
08:49.860 --> 08:50.670
Of course it hurts.

186
08:50.670 --> 08:52.030
I'm not afraid of the pain.

187
08:52.030 --> 08:53.200
I'm worried it'll get infected.

188
08:53.200 --> 08:54.930
I need to keep this foot healthy

189
08:55.200 --> 08:57.330
so I can keep fighting the Kuomintang.

190
08:58.630 --> 08:59.750
Comrade He Long.

191
09:01.030 --> 09:01.960
Why are you here?

192
09:02.260 --> 09:04.720
We came to discuss our next move with you.

193
09:04.750 --> 09:05.550
That's right.

194
09:05.720 --> 09:07.240
I happen to have a plan.

195
09:08.030 --> 09:08.840
Comrade Xiang Xuan,

196
09:08.840 --> 09:10.360
I have a mission for you.

197
09:10.960 --> 09:12.690
Go to the grassland up ahead

198
09:12.720 --> 09:14.960
and bring me five gynura plants

199
09:15.170 --> 09:16.630
and five agrimony plants.

200
09:16.960 --> 09:18.630
Yes. I guarantee to complete the mission,

201
09:18.630 --> 09:19.600
Comrade He Long!

202
09:21.270 --> 09:23.600
-Comrade Xiang Xuan is so cute. -Go ahead.

203
09:24.600 --> 09:25.260
Little guy.

204
09:25.360 --> 09:26.490
Comrade Xiang Xuan.

205
09:27.000 --> 09:27.790
Slow down.

206
09:27.840 --> 09:28.750
Xiang Xuan,

207
09:29.480 --> 09:31.740
do you remember what the herbs look like?

208
09:32.030 --> 09:33.320
I remember.

209
09:33.550 --> 09:35.630
The gynura plants have red seeds and green leaves.

210
09:35.630 --> 09:37.840
Its striped stems are dressed up in colorful clothes.

211
09:37.840 --> 09:38.270
Come here.

212
09:38.270 --> 09:40.480
Its feathery foliage flutters like wings.

213
09:40.480 --> 09:42.150
Clusters of yellow flowers dance in the breeze.

214
09:42.150 --> 09:43.080
Comrade He Long, tell us,

215
09:42.930 --> 09:44.640
[Ren Bishi, Political Commissar of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

216
09:43.270 --> 09:44.960
where are we heading next?

217
09:46.720 --> 09:48.180
Here's what I'm thinking.

218
09:49.310 --> 09:51.520
On March 6, 1936,

219
09:51.970 --> 09:54.760
the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps reached Kuixiang

220
09:55.050 --> 09:58.370
and entered the vast Wumeng Mountain Area.

221
09:58.390 --> 10:00.950
The Kuomintang immediately dispatched

222
10:00.980 --> 10:03.240
3 columns to pursue them northwestward.

223
10:03.600 --> 10:04.720
On March 8,

224
10:05.080 --> 10:06.600
the two corps

225
10:06.620 --> 10:08.750
suddenly turned south from Kuixiang.

226
10:09.270 --> 10:11.750
After defeating part of the enemy force north of Weining,

227
10:11.750 --> 10:13.150
they turned back north.

228
10:13.490 --> 10:15.130
Then, on March 14,

229
10:15.240 --> 10:16.790
they broke through the Kuomintang army's

230
10:16.790 --> 10:19.720
encirclement in the Caishentang area,

231
10:19.870 --> 10:22.340
a stretch of land measuring just 15 square kilometers.

232
10:22.340 --> 10:25.370
They then advanced south through Kuixiang once again,

233
10:25.370 --> 10:27.580
breaking through the Yunnan Army's defensive line.

234
10:27.580 --> 10:30.490
On March 28, 1936,

235
10:30.520 --> 10:33.390
they advanced to the Pan County area on the Yunnan-Guizhou border,

236
10:33.390 --> 10:34.910
where they paused to rest and regroup.

237
10:34.910 --> 10:35.860
After nearly

238
10:36.030 --> 10:39.230
a month on the move and covering more than 500 kilometers,

239
10:39.240 --> 10:40.390
the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps

240
10:40.390 --> 10:44.320
had successfully completed their Wumeng Mountain maneuvering campaign.

241
10:44.320 --> 10:46.910
This was one of the most remarkable campaigns in the history of the

242
10:46.910 --> 10:48.920
2nd and 6th Red Army Corps' Long March.

243
10:48.920 --> 10:50.630
After the three Red Army forces joined together,

244
10:50.630 --> 10:52.360
Mao Zedong met with He Long

245
10:52.380 --> 10:55.170
and praised the campaign.

246
10:56.000 --> 10:56.870
He said,

247
10:57.390 --> 10:59.250
"You set out with more than 10,000 troops,

248
10:59.250 --> 11:01.080
and after all that marching, you still have more than 10,000.

249
11:01.080 --> 11:02.600
You still have more than 10,000 men.

250
11:02.600 --> 11:04.860
That's an extraordinary achievement."

251
11:05.360 --> 11:07.210
While the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps

252
11:07.210 --> 11:10.140
were maneuvering through the Wumeng Mountain Area,

253
11:10.640 --> 11:11.730
in Shanxi,

254
11:12.240 --> 11:15.030
the 1st Front Red Army, during its Eastern Expedition, divided into three routes,

255
11:15.030 --> 11:16.550
cooperated with each other.

256
11:16.550 --> 11:19.150
They repelled several counterattacks by the Jinsui Army

257
11:19.150 --> 11:21.610
and captured large areas of western Shanxi.

258
11:23.480 --> 11:26.750
From March 20 to 27, 1936,

259
11:27.550 --> 11:30.120
the CPC Central Committee held a series of Politburo meetings

260
11:30.120 --> 11:33.750
at several locations in western Shanxi, including

261
11:33.750 --> 11:36.910
Shangxian, Shikou, and Sijiang villages, as well as Shilou County.

262
11:36.910 --> 11:40.000
Mao Zedong repeatedly emphasized that

263
11:40.080 --> 11:41.480
the Communist Party of China

264
11:41.480 --> 11:44.270
stood at the forefront of the national liberation movement.

265
11:44.270 --> 11:45.550
Our task is to

266
11:45.570 --> 11:47.240
seize every moment

267
11:47.270 --> 11:50.130
and win as much support from the people as possible.

268
11:50.790 --> 11:52.750
We call for an end to the civil war and a united front

269
11:52.750 --> 11:54.150
against Japanese aggression.

270
11:54.150 --> 11:55.120
We call for

271
11:55.390 --> 11:58.770
the Red Army to concentrate its forces on the anti-Japanese front in Hebei.

272
11:58.770 --> 11:59.980
We call for

273
12:00.010 --> 12:03.200
the opportunity to fight the Japanese directly as soon as possible.

274
12:03.200 --> 12:07.750
These reflect China's current situation in the war against Japanese aggression.

275
12:07.750 --> 12:09.060
The global situation has entered

276
12:09.060 --> 12:12.180
a new phase of revolution and war.

277
12:12.500 --> 12:15.990
North China has become one of the world's major flashpoints.

278
12:17.120 --> 12:19.320
We haven't gone too far in marching north

279
12:19.320 --> 12:20.840
to fight the Japanese, if anything,

280
12:20.840 --> 12:22.170
we've moved too slowly.

281
12:22.670 --> 12:24.790
Mao Zedong's speeches clarified

282
12:24.840 --> 12:26.640
the Party's theory and strategy

283
12:26.750 --> 12:30.190
and united the Party and the entire army in their resolve to resist Japan.

284
12:30.190 --> 12:31.740
They also laid the political

285
12:31.740 --> 12:33.720
and military groundwork for the nationwide war

286
12:33.720 --> 12:36.400
of resistance that would follow.

287
12:37.320 --> 12:40.280
[Wayaobu, Shaanxi]

288
12:37.670 --> 12:39.150
Leaders! Leaders!

289
12:40.070 --> 12:41.400
A telegram has arrived.

290
12:41.510 --> 12:42.840
Is it another enemy telegram we've decoded?

291
12:41.920 --> 12:45.590
[Wei Yueqiao, Staff Member of the Second Bureau of the Central Military]

292
12:43.320 --> 12:44.350
No, it's not from the enemy.

293
12:44.350 --> 12:46.510
It was forwarded to us by Smedley from France.

294
12:46.510 --> 12:48.120
t's a joint message of congratulations

295
12:48.120 --> 12:49.780
from Mr. Lu Xun and Mr. Mao Dun.

296
12:53.320 --> 12:54.760
In the telegram, they said:

297
12:54.760 --> 12:56.730
"We warmly support

298
12:56.760 --> 12:58.750
the joint call by the CPC and the Chinese Soviet.

299
12:58.750 --> 13:01.000
We believe that only by carrying out their grand plan

300
13:01.000 --> 13:03.550
to resist Japanese aggression and save the nation

301
13:03.550 --> 13:06.680
can the Chinese people achieve liberation and freedom.

302
13:10.670 --> 13:11.600
They also said:

303
13:11.790 --> 13:14.360
"The Red Army's recent victory in Shanxi

304
13:14.670 --> 13:17.340
has proved that even soldiers serving in the traitorous army

305
13:17.340 --> 13:20.790
support this policy advocated by the CCP and the Chinese Soviet

306
13:20.790 --> 13:23.240
Despite living under the iron heel

307
13:23.510 --> 13:25.360
of the warlords, the people of Peiping,

308
13:25.360 --> 13:27.700
Shanghai, Hankou, and Guangzhou

309
13:27.750 --> 13:30.910
have recently launched a powerful anti-Japanese and anti-fascist movement.

310
13:30.910 --> 13:33.720
This shows how strongly people across the country support

311
13:33.720 --> 13:37.180
the CPC and the Chinese Soviet's national salvation program.

312
13:37.910 --> 13:41.080
Brave Red Army commanders and soldiers,

313
13:41.440 --> 13:43.040
your brave fight

314
13:43.240 --> 13:44.640
and your great victories

315
13:44.960 --> 13:47.840
will forever be recorded in the history of China's liberation

316
13:47.840 --> 13:49.630
as one of its most glorious chapters.

317
13:49.630 --> 13:51.670
The people nationwide look forward

318
13:51.670 --> 13:53.030
to your greater victories.

319
13:53.030 --> 13:55.360
People across the country are determined

320
13:55.550 --> 13:56.910
to stand behind you

321
13:57.200 --> 13:58.630
and support you.

322
13:58.960 --> 14:00.490
Every step you take forward

323
14:00.600 --> 14:04.270
will be met with their warm support and welcome."

324
14:05.000 --> 14:06.150
That's wonderful.

325
14:06.840 --> 14:08.640
When we needed support the most,

326
14:08.960 --> 14:10.510
Mr. Lu Xun and Mr. Mao Dun

327
14:10.530 --> 14:13.190
gave us tremendous encouragement and support.

328
14:13.510 --> 14:15.000
This is more than a message of congratulations.

329
14:15.000 --> 14:18.060
It also gives us confidence in our fight against Japan.

330
14:18.550 --> 14:19.080
I think

331
14:19.320 --> 14:21.360
we should forward this telegram

332
14:21.390 --> 14:22.910
to Comrade Zedong as soon as possible,

333
14:22.910 --> 14:25.320
and ask him to pass their message of support

334
14:25.670 --> 14:28.870
to the officers and soldiers taking part in the Eastern Expedition.

335
14:28.870 --> 14:30.360
Also, I think

336
14:31.240 --> 14:33.750
we should send a comrade to Shanghai

337
14:34.030 --> 14:35.960
to contact Mr. Lu Xun, Mr. Mao Dun,

338
14:36.270 --> 14:38.150
and Ms. Soong Ching-ling,

339
14:38.750 --> 14:41.550
rebuild the underground Party organization there,

340
14:41.550 --> 14:44.910
and win the support of progressive figures in areas under Kuomintang control

341
14:44.910 --> 14:47.970
for the Party's Anti-Japanese National United Front.

342
14:49.380 --> 14:50.140
Good.

343
14:54.060 --> 14:57.870
[Yan Xishan's Residence, Taiyuan, Shanxi]

344
14:55.440 --> 14:56.440
I plan to organize

345
14:56.670 --> 14:58.150
the Central Army troops entering Shanxi

346
14:58.150 --> 14:59.480
into the 1st Route Army.

347
14:59.960 --> 15:02.200
Deploy them along the southern section of the Tongpu Railway,

348
15:02.200 --> 15:03.750
and the southeastern Shanxi.

349
15:03.750 --> 15:05.960
Their primary mission is to pursue and destroy the Communist Right Route Army

350
15:05.960 --> 15:08.270
to prevent it from advancing toward Hebei and Henan.

351
15:08.040 --> 15:10.390
[Liang Huazhi, Confidential Secretary of the Taiyuan Pacification Commission of the Kuomintang]

352
15:08.620 --> 15:10.590
As for the columns of the Jinsui Army,

353
15:10.440 --> 15:13.190
[Yan Xishan, Vice Generalissimo of the KMT's Military Affairs Commission, Director of the Taiyuan Pacification Headquarters]

354
15:10.840 --> 15:12.380
they will be organized into the 2nd Route Army,

355
15:12.380 --> 15:14.790
deployed in southwestern and northwestern Shanxi

356
15:14.790 --> 15:16.550
to cut off the retreat routes of the Communist Left Route Army

357
15:16.550 --> 15:17.870
and the Central Route Army.

358
15:17.870 --> 15:18.670
Meanwhile,

359
15:18.880 --> 15:20.610
the Generalissimo has ordered

360
15:20.960 --> 15:24.150
the troops stationed in Luoyang, Tongguan, and Guanzhong

361
15:24.050 --> 15:26.180
[Zhao Daiwen, Chief Advisor of the KMT's Taiyuan Pacification Headquarters]

362
15:24.450 --> 15:25.420
to advance north

363
15:25.690 --> 15:26.510
and block the crossings over the Yellow River,

364
15:26.240 --> 15:27.880
[Guan Linzheng, Division Commander of the 25th Division of the KMT's Central Army]

365
15:26.760 --> 15:28.150
ensuring the main Communist force is cornered

366
15:28.150 --> 15:31.670
and destroyed in the Luliang Mountain Area on the east bank of the Yellow River.

367
15:31.670 --> 15:33.600
Very good.

368
15:33.940 --> 15:35.380
Let's do it this way.

369
15:37.600 --> 15:38.550
Come.

370
15:39.440 --> 15:41.100
Now that the military plans are settled,

371
15:41.100 --> 15:42.760
let's get back to our noodles.

372
15:43.480 --> 15:44.910
Brother Cixiu (Chen Cheng),

373
15:44.910 --> 15:47.060
I know you don't like

374
15:47.090 --> 15:49.330
Shanxi knife-cut noodles.

375
15:49.790 --> 15:52.190
I know you're from Qingtian in Zhejiang,

376
15:52.670 --> 15:55.880
so I had something from your hometown prepared for you.

377
15:56.270 --> 15:56.730
Huazhi.

378
15:56.910 --> 15:58.480
No need, really.

379
15:58.870 --> 16:00.190
Since I'm in Shanxi,

380
16:00.550 --> 16:02.150
I'll eat what the locals eat.

381
16:02.240 --> 16:03.960
I'll have a bowl of your noodles.

382
16:03.960 --> 16:05.560
That's how we do things here.

383
16:07.240 --> 16:08.670
All right, all right.

384
16:10.120 --> 16:10.960
Very well.

385
16:13.000 --> 16:14.040
Thank you.

386
16:15.810 --> 16:16.870
It's so delicious.

387
16:20.490 --> 16:22.970
s the KMT forces launched a joint encirclement

388
16:22.970 --> 16:25.790
campaign against the Red Army's Eastern Expedition forces,

389
16:25.790 --> 16:27.510
the 4th Front Army, in accordance with

390
16:27.510 --> 16:29.080
the plan formulated in early February,

391
16:29.080 --> 16:31.550
"Battle Plan for the Kangding-Daofu-Luhuo Campaign",

392
16:31.550 --> 16:33.720
advanced into northern Xikang.

393
16:33.920 --> 16:36.830
Along the way, they endured extreme cold

394
16:37.360 --> 16:39.260
and crossed Jiajin Mountain,

395
16:39.480 --> 16:41.960
Zheduo Mountain, and other large snow-covered mountains.

396
16:41.960 --> 16:43.930
After suffering heavy casualties,

397
16:43.930 --> 16:45.640
they went on to capture

398
16:45.670 --> 16:48.200
Daofu, Luhuo, and Ganzi in March.

399
16:48.390 --> 16:49.630
By early April,

400
16:50.000 --> 16:52.880
the 4th Front Army had taken control of a vast region stretching from Danba

401
16:52.880 --> 16:54.040
in the east to Ganzi in the west,

402
16:54.040 --> 16:56.000
extending south to Zhanhua and Taining

403
16:56.000 --> 16:58.400
and bordering the grasslands to the north.

404
17:00.630 --> 17:02.790
[Ganzi, Sichuan]

405
17:11.500 --> 17:12.460
Comrade Guotao,

406
17:12.940 --> 17:14.069
you wanted to see me?

407
17:14.460 --> 17:15.720
Commander-in-Chief.

408
17:16.349 --> 17:18.410
He Long and Ren Bishi sent a telegram.

409
17:18.640 --> 17:20.000
The 2nd and 6th Army Corps have arrived

410
17:20.000 --> 17:22.380
at Pan County on the Yunnan-Guizhou border to rest.

411
17:22.380 --> 17:24.020
They're asking for our instructions

412
17:24.020 --> 17:25.280
on their next move.

413
17:30.030 --> 17:33.270
We have little information about

414
17:33.300 --> 17:35.190
recent domestic and international developments.

415
17:35.190 --> 17:36.950
From a strategic standpoint,

416
17:36.970 --> 17:38.900
should we move north immediately?

417
17:39.680 --> 17:40.790
Or...

418
17:41.650 --> 17:41.960
Here.

419
17:41.960 --> 17:42.890
In the future...

420
17:43.020 --> 17:43.740
Come here.

421
17:49.550 --> 17:51.310
If the 1st and 4th Front Armies

422
17:51.330 --> 17:53.460
launch their main advance northward,

423
17:53.480 --> 17:56.220
will our operations south of the Yangtze

424
17:56.790 --> 17:59.350
leave us isolated and vulnerable?

425
17:59.590 --> 18:01.390
It's hard to judge at this point.

426
18:03.350 --> 18:04.960
That's not the case, Comrade Guotao.

427
18:04.960 --> 18:06.550
The Central Committee sent us a telegram earlier,

428
18:06.550 --> 18:08.680
outlining its strategic plan for the 2nd and 6th Army Corps

429
18:08.680 --> 18:10.550
to march north and resist Japanese aggression.

430
18:10.550 --> 18:11.880
Didn't you tell Ren Bishi

431
18:11.880 --> 18:13.480
and Comrade He Long about it?

432
18:14.570 --> 18:15.290
Not yet.

433
18:16.550 --> 18:18.350
This is a matter of great importance.

434
18:18.350 --> 18:19.960
I need to hear your opinion first.

435
18:19.960 --> 18:21.070
Hear my opinion?

436
18:22.200 --> 18:23.720
That's rare.

437
18:24.160 --> 18:27.160
Well, looks like things are finally heating up for me.

438
18:28.000 --> 18:29.260
All the way down south,

439
18:30.240 --> 18:33.270
when have things ever been quiet for you?

440
18:34.720 --> 18:36.200
It's a major decision, after all.

441
18:36.200 --> 18:37.960
Of course I need to discuss it

442
18:38.240 --> 18:39.370
with you first, Commander-in-Chief,

443
18:39.370 --> 18:41.630
so no one can accuse me of acting on my own.

444
18:41.790 --> 18:43.920
I can't afford to take the blame again.

445
18:45.240 --> 18:46.920
Judging from the wording of the telegram,

446
18:46.920 --> 18:48.590
the 2nd and 6th Army Corps are inclined to

447
18:48.590 --> 18:51.350
remain in the Yunnan-Guizhou border region

448
18:51.790 --> 18:53.030
and establish a base area.

449
18:53.030 --> 18:54.000
But I think

450
18:54.400 --> 18:55.790
the Central Committee's overall strategy is

451
18:55.790 --> 18:58.310
to establish the Anti-Japanese National United Front.

452
18:58.310 --> 19:01.070
Marching north to resist Japan is the inevitable course.

453
19:01.070 --> 19:02.360
From a strategic standpoint,

454
19:02.360 --> 19:04.350
rather than have the 2nd and 6th Army Corps remain in the south

455
19:04.350 --> 19:05.480
fighting on their own,

456
19:05.480 --> 19:07.180
they should head north to cross the Jinsha River

457
19:07.180 --> 19:09.120
and join us in the Ganzi area,

458
19:09.640 --> 19:12.570
then we'll march together toward Shaanxi and Gansu.

459
19:12.590 --> 19:13.350
Good.

460
19:14.080 --> 19:15.540
We see things the same way.

461
19:15.960 --> 19:18.030
Then let's send them a telegram

462
19:18.030 --> 19:19.310
in the name of the Red Army Headquarters,

463
19:19.310 --> 19:21.920
suggesting the 2nd and 6th Corps cross the Jinsha River and head north

464
19:21.920 --> 19:24.580
to join forces with us and march north together.

465
19:43.860 --> 19:44.870
Commander-in-Chief.

466
19:44.870 --> 19:45.760
I was just looking for you.

467
19:45.760 --> 19:46.290
Bocheng.

468
19:46.550 --> 19:47.400
What is it?

469
19:47.920 --> 19:49.520
I heard Zhang Guotao sent someone

470
19:49.520 --> 19:50.980
to invite you to a meeting?

471
19:52.270 --> 19:54.160
He wanted my opinion on the

472
19:54.530 --> 19:56.200
next move of the 2nd and 6th Army Corps.

473
19:56.200 --> 19:57.270
What did you say?

474
19:57.830 --> 19:59.310
I suggested the 2nd and 6th Army Corps

475
19:59.310 --> 20:00.640
cross the Jinsha River and head north,

476
20:00.640 --> 20:01.750
and after joining forces with us,

477
20:01.750 --> 20:02.790
we would march north together.

478
20:02.790 --> 20:03.720
Commander-in-Chief.

479
20:03.720 --> 20:07.120
I heard some cadres at the Red Army School talking about this.

480
20:07.440 --> 20:09.100
Zhang Guotao has long decided

481
20:09.590 --> 20:11.750
to have the 2nd and 6th Army Corps march north.

482
20:11.750 --> 20:12.640
In my opinion,

483
20:12.960 --> 20:14.200
he invited you to that meeting,

484
20:14.200 --> 20:15.640
making it look like he was seeking your advice,

485
20:15.640 --> 20:17.880
because he doesn't want to take responsibility.

486
20:17.880 --> 20:18.550
Why does he want the 2nd and 6th Army Corps

487
20:18.550 --> 20:19.920
to march north?

488
20:20.160 --> 20:21.590
Since the southward campaign began,

489
20:21.590 --> 20:23.640
the 4th Front Army has suffered heavy losses.

490
20:23.640 --> 20:25.110
The army once numbered over 80,000,

491
20:25.110 --> 20:27.400
but its numbers have fallen to just over 40,000.

492
20:27.400 --> 20:29.860
Zhang Guotao wants to take this opportunity

493
20:29.930 --> 20:32.730
to bring the 2nd and 6th Army Corps over to his side,

494
20:33.160 --> 20:35.690
so that he can use them to challenge the CPC...

495
20:36.030 --> 20:36.880
Bocheng.

496
20:37.240 --> 20:39.810
I'm not surprised by his little scheme.

497
20:40.920 --> 20:42.400
I have my own reasons for suggesting

498
20:42.400 --> 20:44.310
the 2nd and 6th Army Corps move north.

499
20:44.310 --> 20:45.510
I believe in the Party spirit

500
20:45.510 --> 20:47.350
of Comrade Ren Bishi and Comrade He Long.

501
20:47.350 --> 20:48.920
Having them joining forces with us

502
20:48.920 --> 20:50.640
will only strengthen our unity.

503
20:50.640 --> 20:51.240
Moreover,

504
20:51.260 --> 20:53.200
there will be more voices in alignment with the Central Committee.

505
20:53.200 --> 20:54.160
By then,

506
20:54.890 --> 20:57.480
Zhang Guotao won't be able to stir up trouble.

507
21:04.680 --> 21:07.540
[Pan County, Guizhou]

508
21:11.590 --> 21:12.640
Comrades.

509
21:13.480 --> 21:15.250
The Central Military Commission has replied.

510
21:15.250 --> 21:16.720
They want the 2nd and 6th Army Corps to

511
21:16.720 --> 21:18.510
cross the Jinsha River and head north,

512
21:18.510 --> 21:19.880
proceed to the northern Kang region

513
21:19.880 --> 21:21.260
and join forces with the 4th Front Army.

514
21:21.260 --> 21:23.120
Now, please share your opinions.

515
21:23.760 --> 21:25.500
[Xiao Ke, Captain of the 6th Red Army Corps]

516
21:25.270 --> 21:27.480
Heading north to cross the Jinsha River?

517
21:27.480 --> 21:28.680
Given the vulnerable

518
21:28.880 --> 21:30.350
enemy defenses in this area,

519
21:30.350 --> 21:32.210
we can establish a base area here.

520
21:32.920 --> 21:34.440
Our troops have marched a very long way,

521
21:34.440 --> 21:35.510
and we need time to rest and regroup.

522
21:35.510 --> 21:37.400
Establishing a base here along the Yunnan-Guizhou border

523
21:37.400 --> 21:38.750
would be to our advantage.

524
21:38.750 --> 21:39.860
Going to the northern Kang region

525
21:39.860 --> 21:40.730
means crossing another river

526
21:40.730 --> 21:41.920
and making another long journey.

527
21:41.920 --> 21:44.520
There would be a lot of obstacles along the way.

528
21:46.110 --> 21:48.030
Given the current practical situation,

529
21:48.030 --> 21:50.290
we have a good chance of succeeding here.

530
21:50.880 --> 21:53.550
But from a long-term perspective,

531
21:53.960 --> 21:57.000
marching north to join the 4th Front Army

532
21:57.270 --> 22:00.930
is more in line with the Military Commission's overall strategy.

533
22:01.790 --> 22:03.260
I agree with Commander-in-Chief He Long.

534
22:03.260 --> 22:03.880
Agreed.

535
22:04.000 --> 22:04.510
Agreed.

536
22:04.580 --> 22:06.510
I agree with Commander-in-Chief He Long, too.

537
22:06.510 --> 22:08.840
Now, based on his opinion,

538
22:08.960 --> 22:10.440
I'd like to add a few things.

539
22:10.440 --> 22:11.270
I think,

540
22:11.590 --> 22:14.050
when faced with major strategic decisions,

541
22:14.270 --> 22:15.870
we must not only obey orders,

542
22:16.090 --> 22:17.960
but also keep our priorities in mind.

543
22:17.960 --> 22:19.880
And what is our priority right now?

544
22:19.880 --> 22:20.880
Resisting Japanese aggression.

545
22:20.880 --> 22:22.980
That is not just the priority of the Communist Party

546
22:22.980 --> 22:24.350
and our Red Army.

547
22:24.680 --> 22:27.010
It's the priority for the enitire nation!

548
22:27.410 --> 22:28.810
Our 2nd and 6th Army Corps

549
22:28.920 --> 22:31.400
must not be concerned only with our own immediate interests.

550
22:31.400 --> 22:34.400
We must answer the Military Commission's call with determination

551
22:34.400 --> 22:35.630
and march north without hesitation!

552
22:35.630 --> 22:36.350
Agreed.

553
22:36.830 --> 22:37.570
I agree. We should head north.

554
22:37.570 --> 22:38.670
We should head north.

555
22:38.670 --> 22:39.470
Agreed.

556
22:45.550 --> 22:46.640
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt.

557
22:46.640 --> 22:48.270
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt, you're here.

558
22:48.270 --> 22:49.800
What's the occasion today?

559
22:50.110 --> 22:51.310
It's a special day.

560
22:53.410 --> 22:54.600
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt.

561
22:54.600 --> 22:55.070
Why?

562
22:55.070 --> 22:56.930
You are the main character today.

563
22:57.040 --> 22:58.240
You shouldn't lift a finger.

564
22:58.240 --> 22:58.860
Have a seat.

565
22:58.860 --> 23:00.070
You're our guest of honor today.

566
23:00.070 --> 23:01.070
Come on. Sit down.

567
23:01.270 --> 23:02.110
Have a seat.

568
23:04.000 --> 23:04.860
Guest of honor?

569
23:05.030 --> 23:06.560
You don't have to do a thing.

570
23:06.790 --> 23:07.480
Corps Commander.

571
23:07.480 --> 23:07.880
Why?

572
23:07.900 --> 23:09.630
The mashed potatoes are ready.

573
23:09.830 --> 23:10.350
All right.

574
23:10.350 --> 23:11.470
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt,

575
23:11.470 --> 23:13.780
I made something special for you—

576
23:14.000 --> 23:15.000
mashed potatoes.

577
23:15.030 --> 23:16.310
We don't have any honey here,

578
23:16.310 --> 23:18.030
so you can add a little sugar in it later.

579
23:18.030 --> 23:19.240
It tastes great.

580
23:19.550 --> 23:20.590
Each of them

581
23:20.790 --> 23:23.030
has prepared one of their specialties for you.

582
23:23.030 --> 23:25.030
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt, look,

583
23:25.180 --> 23:26.050
I prepared

584
23:26.080 --> 23:28.490
your favorite cold fish mint stem salad.

585
23:28.680 --> 23:29.920
What's going on?

586
23:30.590 --> 23:32.020
May I know the reason?

587
23:32.590 --> 23:33.750
This special meal

588
23:33.990 --> 23:35.990
is our way of seeing you off.

589
23:39.240 --> 23:40.890
As I understand it,

590
23:41.310 --> 23:43.480
in Chinese, "seeing someone off" can mean two very different things.

591
23:43.480 --> 23:44.940
One is a genuine farewell,

592
23:45.070 --> 23:47.730
and the other is sending someone to their death.

593
23:50.440 --> 23:51.180
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt,

594
23:51.180 --> 23:52.740
you know quite a lot.

595
23:53.310 --> 23:54.070
Don't worry.

596
23:54.130 --> 23:55.240
That's not the kind of farewell

597
23:55.240 --> 23:56.640
you thought it would be.

598
23:57.570 --> 24:00.440
Please, have a seat now, Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt.

599
24:00.440 --> 24:02.200
We're heading north.

600
24:02.440 --> 24:03.240
Now,

601
24:03.270 --> 24:05.240
we're going to keep the promise we made to you,

602
24:05.240 --> 24:06.570
sending you to Kunming,

603
24:06.730 --> 24:08.930
so you can be reunited with your family.

604
24:09.840 --> 24:12.670
I thought you'd say "release,"

605
24:13.120 --> 24:15.580
but instead, you said you were seeing me off.

606
24:15.590 --> 24:16.230
I know.

607
24:16.640 --> 24:18.970
People only see their friends off, right?

608
24:19.170 --> 24:20.490
We're friends now.

609
24:20.770 --> 24:21.870
We're not just friends—

610
24:21.870 --> 24:23.510
we're good friends.

611
24:23.790 --> 24:24.640
Think about it,

612
24:24.640 --> 24:26.790
we've been traveling together for over a year.

613
24:26.790 --> 24:28.110
We crossed five provinces,

614
24:28.110 --> 24:29.510
and walked more than 5,000 kilometers.

615
24:29.510 --> 24:30.960
We've even been

616
24:31.070 --> 24:33.130
pursued by the Kuomintang together.

617
24:33.320 --> 24:35.250
If that's not friendship, what is?

618
24:36.200 --> 24:36.720
Oh, God.

619
24:36.860 --> 24:39.250
I don't know what to say.

620
24:42.070 --> 24:43.270
I want to help out too.

621
24:43.590 --> 24:44.590
Didn't you say

622
24:44.710 --> 24:46.710
those who don't work shouldn't eat?

623
24:48.030 --> 24:50.480
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt, you've made progress again.

624
24:50.480 --> 24:52.060
Come on, Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt.

625
24:52.060 --> 24:53.060
Pound the garlic.

626
24:53.310 --> 24:53.750
Okay.

627
24:55.670 --> 24:56.600
Mr. Zhou,

628
24:56.750 --> 24:58.240
when we camped together last time,

629
24:58.240 --> 25:00.370
you asked me what I thought of Marxism.

630
25:00.830 --> 25:02.690
I hadn't thought it through then.

631
25:02.960 --> 25:05.200
Now I think I have an answer for you.

632
25:05.510 --> 25:06.350
I'm all ears.

633
25:06.550 --> 25:07.380
Tell me.

634
25:08.050 --> 25:10.160
I've been in China for over ten years.

635
25:10.480 --> 25:11.960
Before I met you all,

636
25:12.160 --> 25:13.920
I traveled to many places.

637
25:14.400 --> 25:15.720
I saw so much

638
25:16.200 --> 25:18.310
poverty, suffering, and injustice.

639
25:18.920 --> 25:21.750
whenever I witnessed such suffering, I would ask myself,

640
25:21.750 --> 25:22.590
"Oh, God,

641
25:22.960 --> 25:26.680
how can I help those poor people?"

642
25:27.000 --> 25:28.330
I spent a long time searching for an answer,

643
25:28.330 --> 25:29.850
but never found one.

644
25:30.550 --> 25:32.110
Until I met you all.

645
25:32.510 --> 25:33.640
Just as you said,

646
25:34.270 --> 25:35.550
for more than a year now,

647
25:35.550 --> 25:37.550
we've walked together

648
25:37.880 --> 25:40.510
on what might be the hardest road in the world.

649
25:41.030 --> 25:42.400
I have seen you—

650
25:42.790 --> 25:44.160
people whom the newspapers

651
25:44.160 --> 25:46.290
described as "bandits" or "robbers"—

652
25:46.480 --> 25:49.310
give away your own scarce food and clothing

653
25:49.510 --> 25:50.830
to the poor,

654
25:51.400 --> 25:53.200
help them dig wells,

655
25:53.310 --> 25:54.640
and repair their homes.

656
25:55.110 --> 25:56.640
I have seen you take shelter

657
25:56.640 --> 25:58.370
from air raids in the orchards,

658
25:58.680 --> 26:01.240
where ripe, sweet fruit hung right above your heads,

659
26:01.240 --> 26:02.840
yet not one of you picked any.

660
26:03.310 --> 26:04.480
As far as I know,

661
26:04.880 --> 26:07.340
bandits and robbers don't behave like this.

662
26:08.000 --> 26:09.720
These beautiful moments

663
26:10.110 --> 26:13.090
have left a deep impression on me.

664
26:14.000 --> 26:15.030
Hearing you say that,

665
26:15.030 --> 26:16.560
I also feel deeply touched.

666
26:16.590 --> 26:17.640
In this army,

667
26:18.070 --> 26:20.070
I've never seen anyone smoke opium,

668
26:20.330 --> 26:21.990
nor have I seen anyone gamble.

669
26:22.110 --> 26:23.880
But in the Kuomintang army,

670
26:24.180 --> 26:25.440
both are commonplace.

671
26:25.720 --> 26:27.200
You've suffered so much,

672
26:27.880 --> 26:29.270
yet you remain so optimistic

673
26:29.270 --> 26:30.680
and full of fighting spirit.

674
26:30.680 --> 26:31.550
If I hadn't spent

675
26:31.550 --> 26:32.880
so much time with you,

676
26:33.350 --> 26:35.350
I definitely wouldn't have believed it.

677
26:35.350 --> 26:36.400
Actually,

678
26:36.640 --> 26:38.880
we are people from poor backgrounds.

679
26:39.680 --> 26:40.740
When we're hungry,

680
26:40.960 --> 26:42.310
we need food, just like anyone else.

681
26:42.310 --> 26:43.170
When it's cold,

682
26:43.350 --> 26:44.550
we need clothes, too.

683
26:44.840 --> 26:46.680
And when our feet blister,

684
26:46.830 --> 26:48.870
we feel the pain just like anyone else.

685
26:48.870 --> 26:50.390
If there's anything special about us,

686
26:50.390 --> 26:52.790
it's our unwavering faith in our course.

687
26:53.160 --> 26:54.030
Our goal is

688
26:54.050 --> 26:56.020
for all the people in the world

689
26:56.160 --> 26:57.640
to live better lives.

690
26:57.960 --> 26:58.790
That's why

691
26:58.950 --> 27:01.740
we chose the path of revolution.

692
27:02.110 --> 27:03.840
We won't stop until we've built

693
27:03.920 --> 27:05.240
a new world.

694
27:05.270 --> 27:06.140
Exactly.

695
27:09.510 --> 27:10.270
Mr. Zhou.

696
27:10.480 --> 27:11.480
Last time you said

697
27:11.480 --> 27:13.740
Marxism gives the poor the means to unite

698
27:13.970 --> 27:16.100
and work toward their own liberation.

699
27:16.640 --> 27:18.440
So my answer is,

700
27:18.920 --> 27:20.720
everything you're doing

701
27:21.030 --> 27:22.960
is something God would approve of.

702
27:23.550 --> 27:24.840
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt,

703
27:24.840 --> 27:26.380
you are a man of God.

704
27:26.790 --> 27:27.510
You came to China

705
27:27.510 --> 27:29.160
and witnessed so much suffering.

706
27:29.160 --> 27:31.030
That shows you are also a kind person.

707
27:31.030 --> 27:32.430
Because only kind people

708
27:32.590 --> 27:34.790
can truly see the misfortune of others.

709
27:34.830 --> 27:35.920
And kindness

710
27:36.240 --> 27:37.180
has nothing to do with faith

711
27:37.180 --> 27:38.640
or political affiliation.

712
27:38.640 --> 27:40.800
Whether you follow Marxism,

713
27:40.830 --> 27:41.680
the Three Principles of the People,

714
27:41.680 --> 27:42.660
or your faith in God,

715
27:42.660 --> 27:44.460
we all share this one belief.

716
27:46.270 --> 27:47.310
Mr. Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt,

717
27:47.310 --> 27:49.110
thank you for your recognition.

718
27:49.130 --> 27:51.330
We will always cherish our friendship.

719
27:54.620 --> 27:55.870
Bless China.

720
27:58.180 --> 27:59.260
Bless the Red Army.

721
28:00.750 --> 28:01.550
Come on.

722
28:01.790 --> 28:02.520
Bless China.

723
28:02.590 --> 28:03.050
Cheers.

724
28:03.160 --> 28:04.270
Bless the Red Army!

725
28:08.270 --> 28:10.200
In April 1936,

726
28:10.450 --> 28:12.850
Rudolf Alfred Bosshardt left the Red Army.

727
28:13.200 --> 28:14.480
Later, he wrote a book

728
28:14.500 --> 28:17.350
about his extraordinary journey

729
28:17.350 --> 28:18.470
with the Red Army.

730
28:18.920 --> 28:22.000
It was published in London, UK, in December.

731
28:22.250 --> 28:23.310
It was the first book

732
28:23.310 --> 28:24.870
written by a Westerner

733
28:24.900 --> 28:28.160
to introduce the Red Army's Long March to Western readers.

734
28:28.580 --> 28:29.900
In 2006,

735
28:30.210 --> 28:31.880
Yellow River Press published it

736
28:31.880 --> 28:34.680
under the title "The Restraining Hand:

737
28:34.680 --> 28:38.160
Captivity for Christ in China."

738
28:43.200 --> 28:47.080
[Damaijiao Village, Xi County, Shanxi]

739
28:44.990 --> 28:47.650
Currently, the Central Army and the Jinsui Army

740
28:47.750 --> 28:49.610
have launched a joint offensive,

741
28:49.710 --> 28:51.680
and have captured several crossings along the Yellow River.

742
28:51.680 --> 28:53.410
They are trying to force us into

743
28:53.590 --> 28:55.480
a narrow strip of land on the east bank of the Yellow River

744
28:55.480 --> 28:56.480
to annihilate us.

745
28:56.680 --> 28:58.550
Looking at the situation as a whole,

746
28:58.550 --> 29:00.280
the situation is looking grim.

747
29:00.880 --> 29:02.480
It seems we can no longer force Yan Xishan

748
29:02.480 --> 29:03.350
to let us pass.

749
29:03.960 --> 29:05.510
He's determined to destroy us.

750
29:04.400 --> 29:07.720
[Ye Jianying, Chief of Staff of the Vanguard Army of the Chinese People's Red Army for Resisting Japan]

751
29:05.970 --> 29:08.300
We can't just sit back and let this happen.

752
29:08.510 --> 29:10.680
We need to plan our withdrawal route in advance.

753
29:10.680 --> 29:12.610
Order the Left Route Army and the Right Route Army

754
29:12.610 --> 29:13.870
to gradually converge

755
29:13.930 --> 29:16.230
so we can concentrate our forces against the enemy.

756
29:16.230 --> 29:18.350
The Central Route Army will commit its main force

757
29:18.350 --> 29:21.240
to pin down the enemy between Xi County and Lingshi.

758
29:21.550 --> 29:22.810
Send part of our forces

759
29:23.550 --> 29:24.960
to the area west of Yonghe

760
29:25.310 --> 29:27.550
to break through the enemy's blockade along the Yellow River

761
29:27.550 --> 29:28.920
and keep our route to northern Shaanxi open.

762
29:28.920 --> 29:30.780
Understood. I'll issue the order right away.

763
29:30.780 --> 29:31.650
Wait a minute.

764
29:32.430 --> 29:33.280
Comrades,

765
29:33.880 --> 29:35.750
we've encountered some difficulties

766
29:35.750 --> 29:36.770
in our military operations.

767
29:36.770 --> 29:37.700
But don't worry.

768
29:39.000 --> 29:41.310
After Comrade Luofu arrived in Wayaobu,

769
29:41.740 --> 29:43.300
the Central Politburo held a meeting.

770
29:43.130 --> 29:46.290
[Yang Shangkun, Director of the Political Department of the Red Army's Anti-Japanese Vanguard Army]

771
29:43.850 --> 29:45.200
He briefed us on some encouraging

772
29:45.200 --> 29:46.960
developments in our united front efforts.

773
29:46.960 --> 29:47.750
First,

774
29:49.310 --> 29:52.240
after Comrade Liu Shaoqi arrived at the Northern Bureau,

775
29:52.240 --> 29:54.800
he corrected some of the earlier

776
29:54.830 --> 29:55.960
"Left" errors,

777
29:56.350 --> 29:57.640
helping break the deadlock in our work

778
29:57.640 --> 29:59.550
in areas under Nationalist control.

779
29:59.550 --> 30:00.120
Second,

780
30:01.150 --> 30:02.400
the Central Committee has decided

781
30:02.400 --> 30:04.350
to reassign Comrade Feng Xuefeng from Shanxi

782
30:04.350 --> 30:05.200
to Shanghai.

783
30:05.270 --> 30:07.830
He will serve as a special envoy of the CPC Central Committee,

784
30:07.830 --> 30:10.880
tasked with rebuilding the underground Party organization in Shanghai,

785
30:10.880 --> 30:12.790
while also overseeing literary and artistic work.

786
30:12.790 --> 30:14.100
After arriving in Shanghai,

787
30:14.100 --> 30:15.580
he'll establish contact with Soong Ching-ling

788
30:15.580 --> 30:16.380
and Mr. Lu Xun,

789
30:16.460 --> 30:19.030
seeking to rally progressive figures behind our Party's

790
30:19.030 --> 30:20.830
Anti-Japanese National United Front.

791
30:20.650 --> 30:23.040
[Peng Dehuai, Commander of the Chinese People's Red Army for Resisting Japan]

792
30:21.350 --> 30:22.210
One more thing.

793
30:22.270 --> 30:23.270
Comrade Enlai

794
30:23.400 --> 30:25.640
has already left for Fushi (Yan'an)

795
30:25.750 --> 30:27.410
to begin a formal negotiation

796
30:27.420 --> 30:29.220
with Zhang Xueliang for a truce.

797
30:30.130 --> 30:32.140
Securing an agreement with the Northeastern Army

798
30:32.140 --> 30:32.970
would be just

799
30:33.060 --> 30:35.390
as significant as winning a major battle.

800
30:38.350 --> 30:40.720
After the Red Army troops of the Long March reached northern Shaanxi,

801
30:40.720 --> 30:42.310
Mao Zedong made winning over

802
30:42.310 --> 30:45.510
Zhang Xueliang and the Northeastern Army a top priority.

803
30:45.520 --> 30:47.790
On January 20, 1936,

804
30:48.240 --> 30:49.590
he sent a telegram to Li Kenong,

805
30:49.590 --> 30:52.200
who had gone to Luochuan to negotiate with Zhang Xueliang.

806
30:52.200 --> 30:54.200
The telegram conveyed the Communist Party's sincerity in seeking

807
30:54.200 --> 30:56.880
an alliance with the Northeastern Army against Japan.

808
30:56.880 --> 31:00.680
He pointed out that unless the Northeastern Army found a way forward

809
31:00.680 --> 31:02.440
by resisting Japan and opposing Chiang Kai-shek,

810
31:02.110 --> 31:06.930
[Stop the civil war and unite against Japanese aggression]

811
31:02.510 --> 31:04.510
its future would be in grave danger.

812
31:05.440 --> 31:06.640
On January 25,

813
31:07.350 --> 31:10.000
Mao Zedong, Zhou Enlai, Peng Dehuai,

814
31:10.070 --> 31:12.180
and 17 other Red Army commanders

815
31:12.790 --> 31:13.720
jointly issued:

816
31:13.850 --> 31:17.330
"Letter to All Officers and Soldiers of the Northeastern Army

817
31:17.350 --> 31:20.760
Demanding the Red Army's Readiness to Unite with the Northeast Army to Resist Japan."

818
31:20.760 --> 31:23.260
It reaffirmed the Party's commitment to resisting Japanese aggression.

819
31:23.260 --> 31:25.690
The letter deeply moved Zhang Xueliang.

820
31:25.960 --> 31:29.420
He expressed his willingness to respond to the Communist Party of China's call

821
31:29.420 --> 31:33.350
and work to establish the National Defense Government to resist Japan.

822
31:33.350 --> 31:35.440
During the Eastern Expedition,

823
31:35.590 --> 31:37.500
Mao Zedong maintained contact with Zhang Xueliang

824
31:37.500 --> 31:40.350
through telegrams and intermediaries,

825
31:41.110 --> 31:43.880
continually reinforcing Zhang's resolve to resist Japan.

826
31:43.880 --> 31:46.750
Contacts between the two armies grew increasingly frequent.

827
31:46.750 --> 31:49.160
In early March, Zhang Xueliang proposed

828
31:49.350 --> 31:52.680
meeting Mao Zedong or Zhou Enlai in person for direct talks.

829
31:53.270 --> 31:56.890
Mao Zedong and other Central Committee leaders took the proposal very seriously.

830
31:56.890 --> 31:59.240
They drew up a five-point agenda for the meeting and appointed

831
31:59.240 --> 32:02.510
Zhou Enlai as the Central Committee's plenipotentiary representative.

832
32:02.510 --> 32:04.050
Accompanied by Li Kenong,

833
32:04.160 --> 32:08.230
[Qiao'ergou, Fushi (Now Yan'an), Shaanxi]

834
32:04.190 --> 32:05.430
on April 9, a snowy day,

835
32:05.430 --> 32:07.220
Zhou Enlai set out for Fushi

836
32:07.280 --> 32:09.350
to meet Zhang Xueliang.

837
32:12.110 --> 32:13.240
Mr. Zhou.

838
32:13.490 --> 32:14.050
Welcome.

839
32:14.080 --> 32:15.140
General Xueliang,

840
32:15.400 --> 32:16.480
we finally meet.

841
32:17.270 --> 32:18.720
I've heard you're known as the

842
32:18.720 --> 32:20.820
"Lord of the Magnificent Beard" in the Communist Party.

843
32:20.820 --> 32:23.150
You certainly live up to your reputation.

844
32:24.210 --> 32:26.730
Speaking of which, we used to be fellow students.

845
32:25.320 --> 32:27.180
[Li Kenong, Director General of the Liaison Bureau of the CPC Central Committee]

846
32:27.680 --> 32:28.640
Your teacher,

847
32:29.030 --> 32:30.750
Mr. Zhang Boling of Nankai,

848
32:31.330 --> 32:32.520
was my teacher, too.

849
32:33.160 --> 32:36.030
I never heard you had studied at Nankai.

850
32:36.060 --> 32:38.260
How did you become Mr. Zhang's student?

851
32:38.350 --> 32:40.510
I used to smoke opium

852
32:40.750 --> 32:41.920
and inject morphine.

853
32:41.920 --> 32:43.550
I quit after taking

854
32:43.750 --> 32:44.880
Mr. Zhang's advice.

855
32:45.270 --> 32:46.160
From then on,

856
32:46.400 --> 32:48.330
I've considered him as my teacher.

857
32:48.480 --> 32:49.520
That's remarkably

858
32:49.520 --> 32:52.870
frank of you for our first meeting.

859
32:53.270 --> 32:55.800
Actually, we've been schoolmates all along.

860
32:56.030 --> 32:56.830
Is that so?

861
32:56.960 --> 32:57.460
We both attended

862
32:57.460 --> 32:59.910
Fengtian Dongguan Model School.

863
33:00.380 --> 33:02.540
In 1910, when I was 12,

864
33:03.110 --> 33:04.910
I went to Fengtian with my uncle.

865
33:05.030 --> 33:06.070
That autumn,

866
33:06.220 --> 33:08.280
I enrolled at Dongguan Model School.

867
33:08.680 --> 33:11.750
At that time, the boy who sat beside me was He Zhen.

868
33:12.020 --> 33:14.290
Later, I went on to study at Nankai.

869
33:14.590 --> 33:15.630
Before I left,

870
33:15.860 --> 33:17.510
I gave him a piece of calligraphy that said:

871
33:17.510 --> 33:20.110
"Study for the Rise of China."

872
33:20.570 --> 33:22.200
He's a relative of mine.

873
33:23.360 --> 33:26.160
I saw that piece of calligraphy at his home.

874
33:27.160 --> 33:29.000
But I remember it was signed by

875
33:29.310 --> 33:30.310
Zhou Xiangyu.

876
33:30.600 --> 33:31.710
I am Xiangyu.

877
33:32.160 --> 33:33.400
I see.

878
33:33.830 --> 33:36.110
It's a pity that while you were studying in Fengtian,

879
33:36.110 --> 33:38.370
I was still at a private school back home.

880
33:39.060 --> 33:42.390
I've always kept those words, "Study for the Rise of China,"

881
33:43.320 --> 33:44.710
close to my heart.

882
33:46.480 --> 33:50.160
And only today do I finally get to meet you, Brother Xiangyu.

883
33:50.550 --> 33:51.950
As the Book of Rites says,

884
33:51.960 --> 33:53.990
Those who study under the same teacher are fellow students;

885
33:53.990 --> 33:55.440
those who share the same ideals are friends."

886
33:55.440 --> 33:56.480
From now on,

887
33:56.710 --> 33:59.880
you and I are true friends.

888
34:02.120 --> 34:02.790
Please.

889
34:07.830 --> 34:10.000
There are many spies in Fushi,

890
34:10.360 --> 34:12.110
so I chose this secluded place

891
34:12.190 --> 34:13.360
for our meeting.

892
34:13.550 --> 34:16.010
I couldn't arrange a public welcome for you,

893
34:16.070 --> 34:17.360
so I hope you'll understand.

894
34:17.360 --> 34:18.670
There's no need to apologize.

895
34:18.670 --> 34:19.360
Please.

896
34:27.320 --> 34:28.320
Have some tea.

897
34:40.480 --> 34:41.280
Mr. Zhou,

898
34:42.760 --> 34:44.440
I read the five-point agenda for the meeting

899
34:44.440 --> 34:46.670
drafted by Mr. Mao Zedong the other day.

900
34:47.440 --> 34:48.969
I completely agree with it.

901
34:49.070 --> 34:52.190
It shows your Party's determination to resist Japanese aggression.

902
34:52.190 --> 34:54.480
I also believe that fighting the Communists and resisting Japan

903
34:54.480 --> 34:56.150
are fundamentally incompatible.

904
34:56.150 --> 34:59.760
I fully support your Party's proposal to end the civil war

905
34:59.760 --> 35:01.960
and unite against foreign aggression.

906
35:02.210 --> 35:03.210
If so,

907
35:03.760 --> 35:06.160
that'd be a great blessing for the country.

908
35:07.800 --> 35:09.230
There's just one thing

909
35:10.510 --> 35:11.590
I disagree with.

910
35:12.400 --> 35:13.400
Please, go ahead.

911
35:13.590 --> 35:16.760
Your slogan is "Resist Japan and oppose Chiang."

912
35:17.280 --> 35:18.960
But if we're to unite against Japan,

913
35:18.960 --> 35:22.630
the more forces we can bring together, the better.

914
35:23.880 --> 35:26.320
Generalissimo Chiang holds the highest authority,

915
35:26.320 --> 35:28.670
and I'm officially under his command.

916
35:28.760 --> 35:30.070
If he is excluded

917
35:30.880 --> 35:32.140
from the united front,

918
35:32.750 --> 35:35.880
and if he opposes it on behalf of the Central Government,

919
35:36.230 --> 35:37.000
then...

920
35:38.110 --> 35:40.170
I'll be in a very difficult position.

921
35:42.320 --> 35:45.510
I understand the difficult position you're in.

922
35:46.190 --> 35:48.800
Your point deserves serious consideration.

923
35:49.250 --> 35:52.710
As for your proposal to join forces with Chiang against Japan,

924
35:52.710 --> 35:54.880
I wholeheartedly support it.

925
35:55.230 --> 35:56.630
That's wonderful.

926
35:56.880 --> 35:59.150
When I first made this suggestion, I thought

927
35:59.150 --> 36:00.800
you'd be deeply offended

928
36:01.030 --> 36:02.360
and strongly oppose it.

929
36:03.200 --> 36:04.360
I never expected you

930
36:05.190 --> 36:06.760
to be so open-minded.

931
36:07.960 --> 36:10.360
It's not that I'm personally open-minded.

932
36:10.670 --> 36:11.970
The Communist Party proposed

933
36:11.970 --> 36:14.340
the Anti-Japanese National United Front

934
36:15.220 --> 36:17.970
and made it clear that we would unite

935
36:18.280 --> 36:20.470
with every force willing to resist Japan.

936
36:20.470 --> 36:23.070
Just as we're seeking to do with you, General Xueliang.

937
36:23.070 --> 36:25.330
Yesterday, we were fighting each other.

938
36:25.360 --> 36:29.110
But today, we're sitting together to discuss

939
36:29.130 --> 36:31.400
how we can unite against Japanese aggression.

940
36:31.400 --> 36:32.700
As for Chiang Kai-shek,

941
36:32.700 --> 36:34.100
our attitude is the same.

942
36:34.510 --> 36:37.440
We never excluded him in the first place.

943
36:38.210 --> 36:39.810
But he insists on the policy

944
36:39.830 --> 36:42.730
of "pacifying the interior before resisting foreign aggression"

945
36:42.730 --> 36:44.480
and has undermined the national resistance effort,

946
36:44.480 --> 36:46.230
leaving us with no choice.

947
36:46.760 --> 36:48.550
Even as we speak,

948
36:48.590 --> 36:52.630
his Central Army is fighting alongside the Jinsui Army in Shanxi against

949
36:52.630 --> 36:54.840
the Anti-Japanese Red Army Vanguard on the Eastern Expedition,

950
36:54.840 --> 36:56.840
led by Comrade Mao Zedong.

951
36:57.710 --> 36:58.510
Indeed.

952
36:59.070 --> 37:00.440
That's certainly true.

953
37:02.480 --> 37:03.280
In short,

954
37:03.960 --> 37:05.710
our policy of opposing Chiang while resisting Japan

955
37:05.710 --> 37:07.540
is by no means set in stone.

956
37:08.280 --> 37:11.360
If Chiang Kai-shek is willing to change course,

957
37:11.380 --> 37:13.180
abandon his mistaken policies,

958
37:13.210 --> 37:15.870
and genuinely join the forces resisting Japan,

959
37:16.230 --> 37:19.550
then, in the interest of national salvation,

960
37:19.880 --> 37:22.540
the CPC is prepared to put past conflicts aside.

961
37:22.960 --> 37:26.110
Still, we must not be too optimistic

962
37:26.480 --> 37:28.480
about Chiang Kai-shek's attitude.

963
37:30.630 --> 37:31.630
On this point,

964
37:32.470 --> 37:34.490
we've paid dearly for that lesson.

965
37:37.510 --> 37:38.710
I understand.

966
37:39.810 --> 37:43.670
Generalissimo Chiang's policy of "pacifying the interior before resisting foreign aggression"

967
37:43.670 --> 37:45.480
is leading us down the wrong path.

968
37:45.480 --> 37:47.670
We'll do our best to bring him around.

969
37:48.110 --> 37:49.710
You can put pressure on him from the outside,

970
37:49.710 --> 37:51.630
and I'll try to persuade him from within.

971
37:51.630 --> 37:54.090
We'll definitely get him to change his mind.

972
37:54.880 --> 37:57.430
General Xueliang, I'm deeply touched

973
37:58.510 --> 37:59.990
by your position.

974
38:00.630 --> 38:01.830
Please rest assured.

975
38:02.080 --> 38:04.600
The CPC will do everything in its power

976
38:05.050 --> 38:06.510
to support any effort that

977
38:06.590 --> 38:08.790
advances the cause of resisting Japan.

978
38:09.110 --> 38:10.870
With your help and cooperation,

979
38:10.870 --> 38:12.030
I'm confident things

980
38:12.030 --> 38:14.630
will definitely move in a positive direction.

981
38:18.510 --> 38:19.320
Mr. Zhou,

982
38:20.190 --> 38:21.720
I deeply admire your army's

983
38:21.800 --> 38:23.770
heroic Long March

984
38:23.960 --> 38:27.320
of more than 10,000 kilometres.

985
38:28.230 --> 38:29.780
As a fellow commander,

986
38:30.920 --> 38:32.110
I can only imagine

987
38:34.400 --> 38:36.200
how difficult it must have been.

988
38:37.150 --> 38:39.320
I'd like to know

989
38:39.320 --> 38:40.800
how you managed to overcome

990
38:40.800 --> 38:42.670
so many hardships along the way.

991
38:44.440 --> 38:47.440
Could you tell me how you did it?

992
38:50.170 --> 38:50.880
Certainly.

993
38:51.480 --> 38:52.920
Then allow me

994
38:53.480 --> 38:56.360
to give you a brief account, General Xueliang.

995
39:00.620 --> 39:02.500
After talking through the night,

996
39:03.250 --> 39:04.670
Zhou Enlai gave Zhang Xueliang

997
39:04.670 --> 39:07.550
a detailed account of the Red Army's Long March.

998
39:08.290 --> 39:11.770
The Red Army's ability to maintain its morale in dire straits

999
39:11.800 --> 39:15.070
and eventually reach northern Shaanxi

1000
39:15.090 --> 39:17.690
left a profound impression on Zhang Xueliang.

1001
39:17.840 --> 39:20.630
This not only deepened Zhang Xueliang's understanding

1002
39:20.630 --> 39:22.490
of the Communist Party of China,

1003
39:23.030 --> 39:24.940
but also made him sincerely admire the grand strategy

1004
39:24.940 --> 39:28.870
of the Red Army's Long March to go north to resist Japanese aggression.

1005
39:28.880 --> 39:29.920
This meeting played an

1006
39:29.920 --> 39:33.110
important role in securing Zhang Xueliang's cooperation

1007
39:33.110 --> 39:35.310
with the CPC in the fight against Japan.

1008
39:46.280 --> 39:47.550
After our conversation last night,

1009
39:47.550 --> 39:50.280
I was surprised by how frank

1010
39:50.550 --> 39:52.090
and ambitious you are, Mr. Hanqing.

1011
39:52.090 --> 39:52.900
I believe

1012
39:53.630 --> 39:54.820
you'll definitely become

1013
39:54.820 --> 39:56.620
a true friend of the Communists.

1014
39:56.850 --> 39:58.040
That conversation

1015
39:58.360 --> 40:00.770
brought me sudden clarity.

1016
40:01.410 --> 40:02.770
When I was 16,

1017
40:03.030 --> 40:04.890
I was a typical spoiled young man.

1018
40:05.030 --> 40:08.030
When Mr. Boling (Zhang Boling) gave a speech in Shenyang,

1019
40:08.030 --> 40:08.590
he said,

1020
40:08.840 --> 40:11.170
"China will not perish while we are here."

1021
40:11.290 --> 40:12.820
Those words shook me awake.

1022
40:13.400 --> 40:16.170
From that moment on, it changed the course of my life.

1023
40:16.170 --> 40:18.110
I didn't expect that our conversation

1024
40:18.110 --> 40:20.410
would rekindle that same feeling in me.

1025
40:21.630 --> 40:22.960
I wish we had met sooner.

1026
40:23.360 --> 40:24.690
I wish we had met sooner.

1027
40:25.750 --> 40:26.750
Mr. Hanqing,

1028
40:27.450 --> 40:30.670
you bear the pain of your family's tragedy and the humiliation of our nation,

1029
40:30.670 --> 40:32.510
while facing both praise and condemnation.

1030
40:32.510 --> 40:34.360
You've devoted yourself wholeheartedly

1031
40:34.360 --> 40:35.900
to finding a way forward for our country—

1032
40:35.900 --> 40:38.550
only we Communists can understand and sympathize

1033
40:38.550 --> 40:40.680
with your desire to avenge your family

1034
40:41.280 --> 40:42.320
and help redeem our nation.

1035
40:42.320 --> 40:43.630
And only we

1036
40:43.630 --> 40:45.880
can offer you our sincere help.

1037
40:46.710 --> 40:48.020
Then it's settled.

1038
40:49.400 --> 40:50.880
If you and I take the lead

1039
40:51.050 --> 40:53.250
in uniting the forces resisting Japan,

1040
40:53.380 --> 40:55.640
it won't be hard to change the situation.

1041
40:57.230 --> 40:58.440
It's a deal.

1042
41:04.400 --> 41:06.960
This is the most detailed map of China,

1043
41:07.030 --> 41:10.070
published to mark the 60th anniversary of the Shun Pao.

1044
41:10.070 --> 41:11.800
I'm sure it'll be useful to you.

1045
41:12.880 --> 41:14.030
Gao Fuyuan told me

1046
41:14.030 --> 41:15.590
you've been short of supplies.

1047
41:15.590 --> 41:18.550
I prepared some silver dollars and Chinese legal tender notes

1048
41:18.550 --> 41:19.760
for you as a gift.

1049
41:20.360 --> 41:22.760
I've already given them to your entourage.

1050
41:23.150 --> 41:26.280
As for the radio equipment and medicine you urgently need,

1051
41:26.280 --> 41:27.810
I'll make sure you get them.

1052
41:30.840 --> 41:34.030
Thank you for your generosity, Mr. Hanqing.

1053
41:38.540 --> 41:39.470
Let me take that.

1054
41:46.670 --> 41:49.140
Fushi is a place blessed with good Feng Shui.

1055
41:50.190 --> 41:51.710
I believe Fushi

1056
41:52.070 --> 41:54.130
has a bright future ahead!

1057
41:54.320 --> 41:56.440
I'm sure it will have a bright future!

1058
41:57.560 --> 41:58.810
Until we meet again.

1059
42:00.020 --> 42:01.150
Until we meet again.

1060
42:14.710 --> 42:16.940
[Gao Fuyuan, Former Commander of the 619th Regiment, 107th Division, 67th Army of the Northeastern Army]

1061
42:28.800 --> 42:30.130
Shortly after parting,

1062
42:30.630 --> 42:32.810
Zhou Enlai wrote to Zhang Xueliang:

1063
42:33.840 --> 42:36.520
"A night of conversation, a lifetime of joy.

1064
42:37.240 --> 42:40.010
I shared my impressions with our comrades and sent word to the front.

1065
42:40.010 --> 42:42.500
Everyone agrees that you are a man of exceptional courage and integrity.

1066
42:42.500 --> 42:46.100
This is truly a great blessing for the cause of resisting Japan."

1067
42:47.920 --> 42:49.090
Meanwhile,

1068
42:49.370 --> 42:51.400
thousands of miles away,

1069
42:51.590 --> 42:53.650
the CPC Central Committee's special envoy, Feng Xuefeng,

1070
42:53.650 --> 42:56.440
finally arrived in Shanghai after a long and difficult journey.

1071
42:56.440 --> 42:59.690
There, he went to visit an old friend he hadn't seen in nearly three years—

1072
42:58.220 --> 42:59.490
[Feng Xuefeng, the CPC Central Committee's Special Envoy]

1073
43:00.070 --> 43:01.360
Mr. Lu Xun.

1074
43:01.710 --> 43:03.480
[Lu Xun]
